# Vantage Digital Labs - Unreal Engine Plugin

Official Unreal Engine 5 plugin for Vantage AI-powered NPCs.

![UE5](https://img.shields.io/badge/Unreal_Engine-5.2+-black?logo=unrealengine)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)

## Requirements

- Unreal Engine 5.2+
- C++17 compatible compiler
- Platforms: Windows, Linux, Mac, PS5, Xbox Series X|S

## Installation

### Git Submodule

```bash
cd YourProject/Plugins
git clone https://github.com/vantage-digital-labs/unreal-plugin.git VantageLabs
```

### Manual

1. Download from [Releases](https://github.com/vantage-digital-labs/unreal-plugin/releases)
2. Extract to `YourProject/Plugins/VantageLabs/`
3. Regenerate project files

## Setup

### 1. Enable Plugin

Add to your `.uproject`:

```json
{
  "Plugins": [
    { "Name": "VantageLabs", "Enabled": true }
  ]
}
```

### 2. Configure API Key

In `DefaultEngine.ini`:

```ini
[VantageLabs]
ApiKey=vk_live_your_key_here
Region=Tokyo
EnableVoice=true
DefaultLanguage=ja
```

### 3. Add Module Dependency

In your `Build.cs`:

```csharp
PublicDependencyModuleNames.AddRange(new string[] { "VantageLabs" });
```

## C++ Usage

```cpp
#include "VantageNPC.h"
#include "VantageSubsystem.h"

void AMyNPC::BeginPlay()
{
    Super::BeginPlay();

    UVantageSubsystem* Vantage = GetGameInstance()->GetSubsystem<UVantageSubsystem>();
    Vantage->OnConnected.AddDynamic(this, &AMyNPC::OnVantageReady);
}

void AMyNPC::TalkTo(const FString& PlayerId, const FString& Message)
{
    FVantageChatRequest Request;
    Request.NpcId = TEXT("npc_guard_01");
    Request.PlayerId = PlayerId;
    Request.Message = Message;
    Request.Personality = TEXT("A stern but fair city guard");
    Request.Language = TEXT("ja");

    Request.Context.Add(TEXT("player_reputation"), FString::FromInt(RepSystem->GetRep(PlayerId)));
    Request.Context.Add(TEXT("time_of_day"), WorldState->GetTimeString());

    UVantageSubsystem* Vantage = GetGameInstance()->GetSubsystem<UVantageSubsystem>();
    Vantage->Chat(Request, FOnChatResponse::CreateUObject(this, &AMyNPC::OnResponse));
}

void AMyNPC::OnResponse(const FVantageChatResponse& Response)
{
    // Display dialogue
    DialogueWidget->SetText(Response.Dialogue);

    // Play voice
    if (Response.HasAudio())
    {
        UAudioComponent* Audio = UGameplayStatics::SpawnSound2D(this, nullptr);
        Vantage->StreamAudio(Response.AudioUrl, Audio);
    }

    // Update emotion
    NPCAnimInstance->SetEmotion(Response.Emotion);
}
```

## Blueprint Usage

The plugin provides full Blueprint support:

1. **Vantage Chat** node - Send message to NPC
2. **On Dialogue Response** event - Receive NPC reply
3. **On Emotion Change** event - React to sentiment shifts
4. **On Audio Ready** event - Play voice clips
5. **Set NPC Config** - Configure personality/voice per actor

## Subsystem API

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `Chat(Request, Callback)` | Send chat message |
| `StreamDialogue(Request, OnChunk)` | Real-time streaming |
| `SynthesizeVoice(Text, VoiceId, Lang)` | Standalone TTS |
| `IsConnected()` | WebSocket status |
| `GetLatencyMs()` | Current round-trip time |

## Supported Languages

| Language | Code | Voice Presets |
|----------|------|---------------|
| Japanese | `ja` | 8 voices |
| Korean | `ko` | 6 voices |
| Chinese | `zh` | 6 voices |
| English | `en` | 10 voices |

## Platform Notes

- **Console builds**: WebSocket connections use platform-native TLS
- **Dedicated servers**: Use `VantageServerSubsystem` for headless operation
- **PIE**: Full functionality in Play-In-Editor mode

